            <ArticleTitle>Development of a method for the preparation of zirconium-89 radiolabelled chitosan nanoparticles as an application for leukocyte trafficking with positron emission tomography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0969-8043(17)30741-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.apradiso.2017.09.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Positron Emission Tomography is an attractive imaging modality for monitoring the migration of cells to pathological tissue. We evaluated a new method for radiolabelling leukocytes with zirconium-89 (89Zr) using chitosan nanoparticles (CN, Z-average size 343 ± 210nm and zeta potential +46 ± 4mV) as the carrier. We propose that cell uptake of 89Zr-loaded CN occurred in a two-step process; cell membrane interaction with 89Zr-loaded CN was followed by a slower cell internalisation step.</AbstractText>
